#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"

cat <<EOF
kimballbradford.com — multi-project portfolio on a single DigitalOcean droplet.

Architecture: Traefik reverse proxy (:80/:443) routes by path prefix to
per-project Docker containers. Currently one project:

  live-documents  →  Preact SPA (nginx) + ASP.NET Core API (SQLite)

Scripts in this directory:

  ./help       Show this message

  ./run        Interactive menu to start the site (or parts of it).
               Choose full stack, standalone project, or Vite dev server.
               Ctrl+C to stop.

  ./upload     Build Docker images locally, then deploy to the droplet:
                  1. Build images locally with docker compose build
                  2. Save and compress images to a tar
                  3. SSH to droplet (user: deploy, key: digitalocean)
                  4. Stop any running services
                  5. rsync project files (excludes .git, data/, .env, keys)
                  6. scp and docker load the images
                  7. Start with --no-build (HTTP or HTTPS depending on .env)

Quickstart (local dev):

  # Full site (Traefik + all projects)
  docker compose up --build

  # Live Documents standalone (no Traefik, :80 frontend, :5000 backend)
  cd projects/live-documents && docker compose up --build

  # Frontend only (Vite dev server, :5173, hot reload)
  cd projects/live-documents/frontend && npm run dev

First-time droplet setup (before ./upload):

  The upload script handles first-time setup automatically:
    - Creates the deploy user
    - Installs Docker via get.docker.com
    - Copies the SSH public key

  You just need to create one file on the droplet beforehand:

      ~/kimballbradford-com/.env

  Example .env:

      DOMAIN=kimballbradford.com
      COLLABEDIT_JWT_KEY=<32+ random bytes>
      ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

  For HTTPS, also open port 443 in the DigitalOcean firewall.
  The script skips .env during rsync so it persists across deploys.

Environment:

  .env              Required on the droplet. Copied manually (never uploaded).
  data/             Gitignored. Bind-mounted SQLite databases per project.
  digitalocean      SSH private key for deployment (gitignored).
EOF
